---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  description="Welcome to the astro-markdown-for-agents example site."
>
  <h1>Astro Markdown for Agents</h1>

  <p>
    This example site demonstrates the
    <a href="https://github.com/puralex/astro-markdown-for-agents"
      >astro-markdown-for-agents</a
    > integration. AI agents that send an <code>Accept: text/markdown</code> header
    — or that identify themselves with a known crawler User-Agent — automatically
    receive a clean Markdown version of each page instead of raw HTML.
  </p>

  <h2>Why Markdown for agents?</h2>

  <p>
    Large language models process Markdown far more efficiently than HTML.
    Stripping navigation chrome, scripts, and styling can reduce token usage by
    <strong>80 % or more</strong> on a typical documentation page.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    Cloudflare's built-in Markdown for Agents feature does this automatically on
    paid plans. This integration brings the same capability to any Astro site —
    including the Cloudflare free tier.
  </blockquote>

  <h2>How to test it</h2>

  <p>Start the dev server, then try both of these requests:</p>

  <pre><code># Returns normal HTML
curl http://localhost:4321/

# Returns text/markdown — what an AI agent sees
curl -H "Accept: text/markdown" http://localhost:4321/

# Simulates a known AI crawler
curl -H "User-Agent: GPTBot/1.1" http://localhost:4321/</code></pre>

  <h2>Pages in this example</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="/">Home</a> — this page</li>
    <li><a href="/about">About</a> — explains how the integration works</li>
    <li>
      <a href="/blog/getting-started">Getting Started</a> — a sample blog post
    </li>
  </ul>
</Layout>
